Follow-up from #118 (docs-only fix), NOT a bug - recording an ergonomic trap.

Role::Chat::simple_chat/simple_chat_f/chat take only @messages and hand them to
chat_messages, which turns every non-ref scalar into { role => user, content =>
$string }. So:

    $engine->simple_chat($prompt, reasoning_effort => "high");

silently sends three user messages and drops the control. There is no error, no
warning - the model just answers a conversation that has the words
"reasoning_effort" and "high" appended as separate user turns.

Evidence it is a real trap: the project hit it twice in its OWN documentation
(vLLM.pm SYNOPSIS example 5 and README.md, both fixed under #118), written by
people who know the API.

Possible guards, cheapest first:
  - carp when an odd trailing scalar in @messages exactly matches a key of
    %CANONICAL_CONTROLS in Role::Chat (very cheap, zero false positives in
    practice - nobody sends "reasoning_effort" as a user turn on purpose).
  - carp on any even-length run of trailing plain scalars that looks like a
    kwargs tail.
  - do nothing and rely on docs.

Behaviour change, so it needs a decision before anyone implements it: the first
option is close to free and catches the exact copy-paste mistake, but it is
still a new warning on a hot path and could surprise a legitimate multi-string
simple_chat call. Wants maintainer input, possibly langertha-llm-advisor.

Do not implement without a decision.

Beleg aus der #101-Capture-Vorbereitung (2026-08-24): Engine::AKI komponiert kein Role::ResponseSize (calculate_all_roles: Models, Temperature, SystemPrompt, Chat, Tools, HermesTools). Ein response_size => 16 im Konstruktor wird von Moose stillschweigend akzeptiert und landet nirgends im Wire-Body - die native Wire kennt nur das engine-eigene max_gen_tokens (AKI.pm:121, :243). Gleiche Klasse von stiller Schluckerei wie die simple_chat-kwargs: kein Fehler, keine Warnung, nur ein wirkungsloses Argument. Falls ein Guard kommt, sollte er auch unbekannte/nicht-komponierte Konstruktor-Args abdecken, nicht nur simple_chat.

